    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "A square that has side length $8x$ cm is divided into $y$ rectangles of equal area. What is the area of each of these rectangles?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{64x^2}{y}\\text{ cm}^2$\n\nDivide the square's area by $y$.",
      "worked": "The square's area is its side length squared.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{square}}&=(8x)^2\\\\A_{\\text{square}}&=64x^2\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe rectangles have equal area, so each has area\n\n$$A_{\\text{rectangle}}=\\frac{64x^2}{y}\\text{ cm}^2.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
